meta {
  name: delete blog
  type: http
  seq: 32
}

delete {
  url: {{base_url}}/administrator/blogs/:id/
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: 5c1e8a2f-9d43-4b76-8e0a-1f2c3d4e5a6b
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  Permanently deletes a post. This is the one admin resource that really is
  deleted rather than deactivated -- nothing references a blog post.

  To take a post off the site without losing it, `PATCH` it to
  `{"status": "draft"}` instead.

  ## API example response
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Post deleted."
  }
}
